Looking at the unsatisfiability causes:

1. **`DepositaryReceipt`** (and its subclasses `AmericanDepositaryReceipt`, `EuropeanDepositaryReceipt`, `GlobalDepositaryReceipt`) is defined using `fis:hasUnderlying`, whose `rdfs:domain` was `fis:Derivative`. Since `DepositaryReceipt` is also asserted to be a `Security` (hence `CashInstrument`), and `CashInstrument`/`Derivative` are declared disjoint, this forces unsatisfiability. Fix: widen `hasUnderlying`'s domain to `fis:FinancialInstrument` (the common superclass of both `Derivative` and `CashInstrument`/`Security`), which still supports all existing uses (Option, Future, Swap, DepositaryReceipt).

2. **`EquityWarrant`** is equivalent to an `Option` (⊆ `Derivative`) but was also asserted `rdfs:subClassOf fis:HybridSecurity` (⊆ `Security` ⊆ `CashInstrument`), conflicting with the `CashInstrument`/`Derivative` disjointness. Fix: drop the redundant `HybridSecurity` superclass assertion (the equivalence to `Option ⊓ ...` already fully characterizes it).

3. **`TreasuryBill`** uses `fis:hasCouponRate`, whose domain was `fis:Bond`, forcing `TreasuryBill` (a `MoneyMarketInstrument`) to also be a `Bond` — contradicting `Bond owl:disjointWith MoneyMarketInstrument`. Fix: widen `hasCouponRate`'s domain to `fis:DebtSecurity` (covers both `Bond` and `MoneyMarketInstrument` without weakening any other axiom).

```turtle
@prefix fis: <http://example.org/onto/securities#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/onto/securities> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Securities and Financial Instruments Ontology" ;
    rdfs:comment "An OWL ontology modelling securities, debt, equity, hybrid and derivative financial instruments, investment funds, issuers, investors and markets, built strictly from the supplied corpus." .

fis:AsianOption a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Payoff determined by the average underlying price over a preset period." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf fis:Option .

fis:AssessmentBond a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Promises repayment based on property tax assessments; generally considered a form of general obligation bond." ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( fis:GeneralObligationBond [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty fis:hasRepaymentSource ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom fis:PropertyTaxAssessment ] ) ] .

fis:BalancedFund a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hybrid fund" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blends equities and fixed income in a single portfolio." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf fis:MutualFund .

fis:BarrierOption a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Underlying price must pass a barrier level before it can be exercised." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf fis:Option .

fis:BearerBond a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An official certificate issued without a named holder; claimable by whoever possesses it." ;
